From 7465838fbaa9c77f25707e409b497337a1777775 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:57:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] testsuite: microblaze supports sync_int_long

MicroBlaze has lwx/swx and an atomic_compare_and_swapsi pattern, so
32-bit __sync and __atomic operations are expanded inline with no
library calls (read-modify-write operations as lwx/swx loops).  The
target was not in check_effective_target_sync_int_long, so the generic
atomic tests were UNSUPPORTED.  With it, 21 more tests run and pass
on microblaze-elf and microblazeel-elf: 19 in gcc.dg, 1 in
gcc.dg/torture, and gcc.dg/pr86314.c through sync_int_long_stack
(149 PASS, 0 FAIL on each).  Three stay UNSUPPORTED for other reasons:
two are x86-only and one needs _BitInt.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* lib/target-supports.exp (check_effective_target_sync_int_long):
	Add microblaze.
---
 gcc/testsuite/lib/target-supports.exp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/lib/target-supports.exp b/gcc/testsuite/lib/target-supports.exp
index 9e69020e7..de7960dd2 100644
--- a/gcc/testsuite/lib/target-supports.exp
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/lib/target-supports.exp
@@ -11039,6 +11039,7 @@ proc check_effective_target_sync_int_long { } {
 	     || ([istarget sparc*-*-*] && [check_effective_target_sparc_v9])
 	     || ([istarget arc*-*-*] && [check_effective_target_arc_atomic])
 	     || [check_effective_target_mips_llsc]
+	     || [istarget microblaze*-*-*]
 	     || [istarget nvptx*-*-*]
 	     || ([istarget xtensa*-*-*] && [check_effective_target_xtensa_atomic])
 	 }}]
